rd:Thur_Anime_Discussion_Thread a crmdig:D1_Digital_Object ;
    crm:P2_has_type schema1:WebPage ;
    schema1:url "https://www.reddit.com/r/anime/comments/pbnr5u/araburu_kisetsu_no_otomedomo_yo_thursday_anime/"^^xsd:anyURI .

rd:GoodReadsReview a r:Discourse_Act ;
    crm:P129_is_about rd:goodReadsBook ;
    crm:P2_has_type r:Evaluation ;
    schema1:text """This was a great book, definitely one of the more unique 40k entries. In it, I found humour, pathos, tension and catharsis. However, some of the military conflict sections significantly slowed it down for me.

The driver of this novel is the relationship between Trazyn the Infinite and Orikan the Diviner. The scenes in which they converse are by far the most compelling, and I think I was a little disappointed that we didn't get more of them (despite them taking up perhaps half of the novel).

I don't think it's prudent or advisable to give a history of the Necron race for context in this review. If you are interested in Necrons, this is possibly the best work of fiction you could ask for that explores their nature.

I've seen people say this stands alone as a good sci-fi novel, but I'm not sure that it would. I might give it to my dad to read and see if he is able to follow it - it would be an interesting experiment.""" ;
    r:encoded_by rd:GoodReadsReview_Post .

